. do test_reachcheck.do 

. * test_reachcheck.do -- behavioral contract for reachcheck
. * run: stata-mp -b do test_reachcheck.do ; grep for ALL TESTS PASSED
. clear all

. adopath ++ "`c(pwd)'"
  [1]              "/Users/ebooth/Documents/GitHub/Book Manuscript:Applied Eval
> uation-Stata/code/reachcheck"
  [2]  (BASE)      "/Applications/StataNow/ado/base/"
  [3]  (SITE)      "/Applications/StataNow/ado/site/"
  [4]              "."
  [5]  (PERSONAL)  "/Users/ebooth/Documents/Stata/ado/personal/"
  [6]  (PLUS)      "/Users/ebooth/Library/Application Support/Stata/ado/plus/"
  [7]  (OLDPLACE)  "~/ado/"

. set varabbrev off

. 
. * --- (1) basic run on nlsw88 race, percentages ---------------------------
. sysuse nlsw88, clear
(NLSW, 1988 extract)

. quietly count if !missing(race)

. local NN = r(N)

. forvalues k = 1/3 {
  2.     quietly count if race == `k'
  3.     local n`k' = r(N)
  4.     local p`k' = 100*r(N)/`NN'
  5. }

. reachcheck race, target(70 20 10)

Reach check: race (N = 2246 respondents)
------------------------------------------------------------
category              sample %  target %   gap pp   ratio
------------------------------------------------------------
White                     72.9      70.0      2.9    1.04
Black                     26.0      20.0      6.0    1.30
Other                      1.2      10.0     -8.8    0.12
------------------------------------------------------------
largest gap: -8.8 pp on Other
goodness of fit vs target: chi2(2) =  218.1, p = 0.0000

The responding sample is off its target by more than 5 pp.
Consider raking to the target margins (ipfraking) and, either way,
report the gap beside the response rate.

. assert r(N) == `NN'

. matrix T = r(table)

. assert abs(T[1,1] - `p1') < .01

. assert abs(T[2,1] - `p2') < .01

. assert abs(T[3,1] - `p3') < .01

. assert abs(T[1,2] - 70) < .001 & abs(T[2,2] - 20) < .001 & abs(T[3,2] - 10) <
>  .001

. * the largest |gap| among the three, with its sign
. local g1 = `p1' - 70

. local g2 = `p2' - 20

. local g3 = `p3' - 10

. local want = `g1'

. if abs(`g2') > abs(`want') local want = `g2'

. if abs(`g3') > abs(`want') local want = `g3'

. assert abs(r(maxgap) - (`want')) < .01

. 
. * --- (2) shares auto-detect gives identical answers ----------------------
. reachcheck race, target(.70 .20 .10) noreport

. assert abs(r(maxgap) - (`want')) < .01

. 
. * --- (3) category-count mismatch errors cleanly --------------------------
. capture noisily reachcheck race, target(70 30)
reachcheck: race has 3 categories in the sample but target() lists 2 values
  sample categories: 1 2 3

. assert _rc == 198

. 
. * --- (4) nonsense target sum errors cleanly ------------------------------
. capture noisily reachcheck race, target(10 10 10)
reachcheck: target() sums to 30.000; expected shares summing to 1 or percentage
> s summing to 100

. assert _rc == 198

. 
. * --- (5) if restriction honored ------------------------------------------
. quietly count if collgrad == 1 & !missing(race)

. local nsub = r(N)

. reachcheck race if collgrad == 1, target(80 15 5) noreport

. assert r(N) == `nsub'

. 
. * --- (6) perfect target gives chi2 ~ 0 and tiny maxgap -------------------
. reachcheck race, target(`p1' `p2' `p3') noreport

. assert abs(r(maxgap)) < .01

. assert r(chi2) < .001

. 
. di as res "ALL TESTS PASSED"
ALL TESTS PASSED

. 
